Dear Luc=C3=ADa,

NOTICE OF DELAY EVENT =E2=80=94 CLAUSE 9.2

I write to give formal notice under clause 9.2 of the Supply and Installation=
 Agreement dated 4 November 2024, as amended and restated on 20 January 2025.

On Tuesday 18 February 2025, while setting out the sorter supports in Bay 3, =
Tomasz W=C3=B3jcik found that the floor slab between grid lines C4 and C7 is =
visibly out of level. We instructed Levantina Topograf=C3=ADa SL to survey th=
e slab the following day. Their report LT-2025-0218 is attached. It records a=
 maximum deviation of 18 mm over 3 m, centred on grid line C5, against the to=
lerance of 5 mm over 3 m required by clause 6.2 of the Agreement. The deviati=
on exceeds the =C2=B120 mm adjustment range of the sorter supports once the h=
igh point at C7 is taken into account.

Delay Event: failure of the Site to comply with clause 6.2 (clause 9.1(b)).

Likely effect: the sorter supports in zone C4=E2=80=93C7 cannot be set until =
the slab has been re-levelled. Our programme shows this activity starting on =
24 February 2025 on the critical path. Based on Levantina's estimate of seven=
 days for screed application and curing, plus mobilisation, we currently esti=
mate a delay to Mechanical Completion and Practical Completion of 14 days, su=
bject to the method of re-levelling Brisamar elects.

Extension of time claimed: 14 days, to be confirmed once the re-levelling met=
hod is agreed.

We have today issued Change Order CO-3 (re-level Bay 3 floor slab) for =E2=82=
=AC48,000 and 14 days, which proposes grinding the high points and a self-lev=
elling screed. Please countersign CO-3 under clause 5.3, or instruct an alter=
native, as soon as possible. We can continue installation in Bays 1 and 2 and=
 in the remaining zones of Bay 3 in the meantime.

I should also flag that the permanent 400A supply under clause 6.4 was due on=
 7 February 2025 and is not yet available. We will keep this under review.

Kind regards,

Priya Nair
Project Manager, Tidewell Fabrication Ltd
